                        "output_text":  "# README.md Review — Token Prompt Compiler\n\nI reviewed the README. Here are 3 small, concrete improvements:\n\n---\n\n## 1. Broken language-switcher link\n\n```text\n**English** | [??](#??)\n```\n\nBoth the display text and the anchor are garbled. The Chinese section header is `## ??`, so even after fixing text, the anchor won\u0027t work because Markdown renders the non-ASCII header unpredictably.\n\n**Fix:** Add an explicit anchor on the Chinese section and link to it:\n\n```markdown\n**English** | [中文](#chinese-版本)\n```\n\nAnd above the Chinese section:\n\n```markdown\n\u003ca id=\"chinese-版本\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\n## 中文版本\n```\n\n(This also fixes the garbled header. Currently it shows `## ??` — presumably meant to be `## 中文版本`.)\n\n---\n\n## 2. Duplicate spec references cause confusion\n\nThe \"Output Format\" section says:\n\n\u003e For full field semantics, see [`SPEC.md`](SPEC.md) and [`references/spec.md`](references/spec.md).\n\nThe reader can\u0027t tell which is canonical or how they differ. Two links to what appear to be the same document adds friction.\n\n**Fix:** Either remove one, or distinguish them:\n\n```markdown\nFor full field semantics, see [`SPEC.md`](SPEC.md).\nFor deeper design rationale, see [`references/spec.md`](references/spec.md).\n```\n\n---\n\n## 3. Installation buries the non-Codex path\n\nThe project claims to be model-agnostic, but the \"Installation\" section is entirely Codex-focused. The only non-Codex instruction is buried as the last sentence.\n\n**Fix:** Add a short subsection header before the Codex-specific steps so skimmers can find the general path:\n\n```markdown\n## Installation\n\n### General (any model)\n\nCopy the `Machine Task Packet` format from this README or `SKILL.md` into your model\u0027s system/project instructions.\n\n### Codex skill\n\nClone this repository into your Codex skills directory:\n...\n```\n\n---\n\n## Summary\n\n| # | Problem | What to do |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Broken `[??](#??)` link + garbled Chinese header | Add explicit anchor and fix header text |\n| 2 | `SPEC.md` and `references/spec.md` linked identically | Distinguish or deduplicate |\n| 3 | Installation assumes Codex-first | Add a \"General\" subsection before Codex steps |\n\nAll three are small (one-line to two-line changes) and improve readability without adding much token weight.",
